WEBVTT

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.570
Missing?

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.840
<b>Missing: Kumashiro Maya</b>

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.540
I haven't been able to reach
her since last night.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.150
And she's been missing for several days.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.130
<b>Missing: Naruse Kozue</b>

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.890
Naruse-kun's parents said she was
absent because she was sick.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.010
And she sometimes vanishes,
saying she's going on "spiritual training."

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.610
Her parents weren't worried.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.670
But if she doesn't come home
after a few days...

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.250
So please, Abe-sensei...

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.810
Help me look for the missing
principal and student!

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.970
W-We should split up, I think...

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.110
That principal is sticking
her head in things again.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.260
Curiosity killed the cat.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:10.580
But what's the point of seducing him?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.670
I...

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.420
Is it wrong for me to fall
in love with someone?

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.310
Not at all...

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.020
<b>Missing Persons Search Group</b>

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.510
What's going on...

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.540
Oh, you're a teacher at Occult Academy!

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.570
I heard you've got problems there, too.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.690
One of your students vanished?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.240
Y-Yes...

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.670
We're doing all we can to find her.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:24.140
I'm sure she'll turn up.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.310
Th-Thank you.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:30.630
<i>I guess even that weird-ass academy
is a part of the local culture.</i>

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.350
Abe-sensei?

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.560
Mikaze-san?

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.430
You're helping out here?

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.030
I was thinking that there's not much for
me to do, but I should try to help...

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.410
Would you like to look for them in the car?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.830
Um...

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.670
Let's go to Nagano City.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.540
I see. Understood.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.970
Someone said they saw a person
like that at Minami-Kamiyama.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.560
At Minami-Kamiyama...

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.020
They've been right under our
noses the whole time.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.550
What's wrong?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.720
I felt like I saw someone back there.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.970
Amato Shrine?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.280
Let's go check it out.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.000
An old tomb?

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:57.940
No one's here.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.450
You're right.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.400
I guess I imagined it!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.330
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.580
No! I am.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.450
I can hear the wind.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.540
I'm scared.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.270
I-It's okay!

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.830
Maybe inside here...

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:49.840
The missing people could be in here,
waiting for us to save them.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.680
But what a shame!

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.240
If I had a light,
I could go rescue them.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.820
If only I had a light...

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.540
Where'd you get those?

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:01.730
There it is!

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.730
Well, you think you can
find the new principal?

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.800
I can feel a faint presence.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.700
This way.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.240
Sensei...

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.240
It's all right.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:24.470
I'm with you.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.370
I'm sorry!

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.400
You're always so kind to me.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.620
I'll always be kind to you.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.700
Then, could we hold hands?

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.130
I might trip again...

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.760
Y-Yeah.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.840
I-I wonder who made this.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.800
They say Minami-Kamiyama is a pyramid.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.700
I heard that, geologically,
it's a strange mountain.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:02.040
And it was the epicenter of the
Matsushiro Earthquake swarm.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.810
U-Uh...

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.390
Some unknown power may be at work here.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.570
A-An unknown power?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.320
Yes! Like a spiritual power!

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.910
Spirits, huh?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.750
"His legs are as the wind."

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.460
"His eyes are clear."

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.840
"His voice softly dances on the wind."

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:38.010
"And he takes my hand and
gently dances with me."

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.020
"We dance... We dance on forever,

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.490
a dance that makes the
very angels jealous."

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.880
Ow...

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.360
Mikaze-san?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.560
Mikaze-san!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.230
Oh, man...
She got left behind...

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.790
Which way did I come from?

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:12.050
Mikaze-san!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.810
Mikaze-san, where are you?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.950
There she is.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.520
You scared me...

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.030
May-

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.910
What was that for?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.180
Don't say my name.
It creeps me out!

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.630
Everyone's looking for you!

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:46.020
What are you doing down here?

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:50.010
I was attacked by a monster
and ran down here.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.820
A monster?

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.300
In the Zouzan Bunker.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.880
No way... An occul-

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.280
I'm sorry.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.410
But what do you mean, a monster?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.470
Is this cave part of the bunker?

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:06.150
It's not. It's older.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.190
Then maybe it's a pyramid?

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.290
Oh, you mean the Minakamiya
Pyramid theory?

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.290
That was Tayama Omoikane's theory.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.370
At first, before the war,

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.340
it was Sakai Katsutoki who claimed

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:20.530
that there were pyramids in Japan, too.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.110
He said they were recorded
in the Takeuchi Scrolls,

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.750
and the Japanese word "hiramitsuto"
was the origin of the word.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.960
He said that Ashitake Mountain
was one of them...

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.510
Wh-What?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.680
I'm just saying that there is such a theory!

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.040
So...

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.040
Yes?

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.900
Which way is the exit?

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.030
Are you maybe-

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.760
Shut up and just tell me!

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:45.930
I got lost, too.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.110
Which way's the exit?

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.110
I said I don't know.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:02.870
And are you sure you should be
leaving this Mikaze-san alone?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.080
That's not what's happening.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.880
What's that?

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.430
Wh-What is this?

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.540
What is this?

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.200
The World Tree?

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.060
World Tree?

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.410
It's called the World Tree
or the Universal Tree.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:51.040
Every mythology in the world has
a tale about a gigantic tree.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.050
The Yggdrasil of Northern Europe.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.960
The Saxon's Irminsul.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.540
The Fusang of Chinese myth.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:03.110
Even Japanese mythology
talks about a massive tree,

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.660
of which it's said, when the
morning sun strikes it, its shadow

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.480
stretches to Awaji Island.
And when the evening sun hits it,

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.310
its shadow reaches past
Takayasu Mountain.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:13.160
It's the tree at the center of the world,

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:15.080
the tree upon which the
very universe hangs!

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:18.030
This is the source of Minami-Kamiyama's power.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.980
The pyramid was built to protect it!

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.780
Could this be Nostradamus's Key?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.420
I'm sure of it!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.460
No good.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:37.420
In 2012, this whole mountain's blown up.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:42.380
Where is Nostradamus's Key?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.430
Bunmei?

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.490
What are you doing?

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:54.580
Are you all-

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.910
What is this?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.750
It stinks!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.290
It's crap!

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.280
It's a massive pile of crap!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.430
Why is there a massive pile of crap here?

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.920
Number 5?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.390
This is what the guy before me use-

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:20.340
Stay back!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.130
You stink, and you're not getting within
a three-meter radius of me!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.640
No!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.560
This belonged to the guy before me!

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.650
No one eats cell phones!

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:30.310
N-No. He was eaten along with it...

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.230
What was that sound?

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.100
It's that monster.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:37.900
Be careful.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.410
Stay three meters away!

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.790
The signal's gotten stronger.

00:12:58.260 --> 00:12:59.840
There's something around here.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.280
...three meters...

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.580
Did we imagine that?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.320
I guess we're okay now.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.680
Don't find out by kicking people!

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.400
What if it were still around here?

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.200
You're a guy.
Stop being a wuss!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.350
Humanity depends on you, right?

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:32.870
Isn't your mission to save the future?!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.750
Don't you have any futuristic weapons?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.670
Isn't this what your psychic abilities are for?

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.830
If you're a top-class psychokinetic,

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.960
then do something about
that stupid monster!

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.660
Sorry.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.130
That was a lie.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:48.260
It was a lie.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.560
A lie.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:51.300
What?

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:11.470
I saw you press it on the ground.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.260
What?

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.270
It was a fraud.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:19.230
Donations... Donations.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.410
I'm sorry!

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.620
I don't have any protection money for you!

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.040
Please don't take my money!

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.620
Are you Uchida Bunmei?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.570
N-No. I'm Fumiaki.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.160
It doesn't matter.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.320
From now on, you're #6.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.610
What is your mission?

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.070
Stopping the Nostradamus Prophecies.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:58.840
If we find Nostradamus's Key and destroy it,
you can save humanity.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:02.290
But we've underestimated Occult Academy.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.170
I'm being chased by a monster,
a monster I've never seen before.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.750
I can't handle it with pyrokinesis.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:09.480
Forget about the key!

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:10.770
Hurry!

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:12.770
No!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.560
I don't want to go where there's a monster!

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.650
You don't have a choice!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.330
No! No!

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:28.400
Nor do we, #6!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.070
You're all we have left!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:34.240
Then take better care of me!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.940
We're counting on you.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.330
...is how it really was.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.040
Hey... Don't leave me here.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.010
Three meters!

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.740
You can't use any psychic powers,
and you get lost in caves.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.800
You're a worthless time agent.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.550
And you stink.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:01.740
Hey, what was that monster?

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.970
The tengu.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.920
Most likely, that's a mothman,

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:07.330
a type of UMA.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.650
It was first recorded in America.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.820
It's a mysterious animal that resembles
a human with giant wings.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:17.370
The tengu was actually a mothman.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.030
A tengu that eats people, huh?

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:29.300
<i>This book contains defensive spells to protect
you from attacks by all of my enemies.</i>

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.390
Is there a spell to protect
against a mothman?

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.680
Wh-What? What?

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:43.920
This is awful...

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.000
What's that?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:50.590
Hey!

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:59.170
Kozue?!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:21.700
What?

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:22.810
What happened?

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:23.420
Shut up!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:34.380
I said, what happened?

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.620
What? What's going on?

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:48.960
No...

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:53.550
No! No!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.090
<i>No!</i>

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.220
No! No! No!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.840
No! No! No!

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:01.930
No!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:05.810
<i>No!</i>

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.230
But... I'm alive...

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.080
I'm alive.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:27.260
I'm... I'm...

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:31.180
I'm saved!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:37.460
Spell... Spell...

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.840
Smile!

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.250
The SDF is here.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.710
I'm the one who found her.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:15.500
JK!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.320
They're not it, either, huh?

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.200
There's no end to them.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.490
Do they have a particular weakness?

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:41.840
I guess I'll try it.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.290
Why did you bring that?

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.460
Music is my life.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:07.050
Real moths don't like sound made
at a certain frequency.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.100
Okay!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.720
Now's our chance!

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:26.680
It's so wonderful to be alive...

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.910
Are you trying to kill me?

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:45.640
Were they sealed in?

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:49.720
Let's get back to the academy.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.450
W-Wait a second!

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.260
Why don't you apologize?

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.060
I almost die...

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:03.530
Coward.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.450
Sensei!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:16.710
Mikaze-san!

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:22.050
I was just about to look for you.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:24.520
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:26.680
If you're safe, that's all that matters.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.430
I didn't see you when I took out
the tengu, so I was concerned.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.050
You got rid of the tengu?

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:39.610
Yeah. I saved the missing student and
sent her back to the academy just now.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.270
Wow!

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.670
You can do anything!

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:45.960
No. It was nothing.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:56.160
Come in.

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.540
The caves are sealed.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.620
I see.

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:01.630
Good work.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:03.830
Anyway...

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:07.050
That principal is a lot of trouble.

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:49.320
Yes.

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:50.330
I was a liar.

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:52.210
"A prince on a white horse,
riding down on a sunbeam!"

00:23:52.210 --> 00:23:53.890
I lost my psychic powers ages ago,

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:55.250
<b>Minorun-chi</b>

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:55.450
and I was forced, against my will,
to go into the past!

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.260
"In an instant, my heart was his."

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:59.010
I thought I'd fallen in love at
first sight with Mikaze-san.

00:23:59.010 --> 00:23:59.950
"Don't look at anyone but me!"

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:02.950
And then I ran away...
Leaving her, Maya, and Naruse behind!

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:04.180
